WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:25.042
Oh, hello. Welcome to our home. I'm Jo March and I'm here to share with you a little about the story you are going to read.

2
00:00:25.043 --> 00:00:28.833
As you may know, it is entitled Little Women.

3
00:00:28.834 --> 00:00:35.645
It's a story about my family─well, more specifically, about me and my three sisters:

4
00:00:35.646 --> 00:00:43.134
Meg, who is the oldest; Beth, who is a couple of years younger than me; and the baby of the family, Amy.

5
00:00:43.135 --> 00:00:51.709
Our story is based on the true-life story of the author, Louisa May Alcott, who also had three sisters.

6
00:00:51.710 --> 00:00:57.213
Louisa May Alcott was born on November 29, 1832.

7
00:00:57.214 --> 00:01:02.102
Like me, she was the second daughter in a family of four girls.

8
00:01:02.103 --> 00:01:06.505
Louisa grew up in Concord, Massachusetts, USA.

9
00:01:06.506 --> 00:01:10.175
From a young age, Louisa loved to write.

10
00:01:10.176 --> 00:01:14.445
She wrote poetry and even several thrillers, believe it or not.

11
00:01:14.446 --> 00:01:21.953
She was also an avid reader, fueling her imagination with works from Shakespeare to Charlotte Bronte.

12
00:01:21.954 --> 00:01:28.174
As you read Little Women, you may see a strong resemblance between my character and Louisa.

13
00:01:28.175 --> 00:01:33.793
In fact, according to Louisa, she did indeed base my character on herself,

14
00:01:33.794 --> 00:01:42.104
while her real sisters─Anna, Lizzie, and May─are depicted by Meg, Beth, and Amy respectively.

15
00:01:42.105 --> 00:01:45.522
Little Women was published in 1868.

16
00:01:45.523 --> 00:01:49.063
The story is set during the American Civil War.

17
00:01:49.064 --> 00:01:53.803
Father is away at war, not as a soldier, but as a chaplain.

18
00:01:53.804 --> 00:02:01.936
He is a very thoughtful, kind man, who instills in us, his daughters, a strong sense of morals and family values.

19
00:02:01.937 --> 00:02:09.689
At one time Father used to be very rich but now, after the war, our family is struggling financially.

20
00:02:09.690 --> 00:02:13.484
Mother is the most loving, caring person in the world.

21
00:02:13.485 --> 00:02:19.741
She is not perfect, but she makes every effort to help us girls learn life's important lessons,

22
00:02:19.742 --> 00:02:24.822
as well as treasure the moments we share together as a family.

23
00:02:24.823 --> 00:02:33.550
My sister Meg is a lovely person who has a strong sense of responsibility and looks after her younger sisters.

24
00:02:33.551 --> 00:02:38.167
Meg does have her faults, though, and one of them is vanity.

25
00:02:38.168 --> 00:02:43.762
She longs to have fashionable, pretty things, as most girls do.

26
00:02:43.763 --> 00:02:49.517
But what can one do if family finances don't permit such treats?

27
00:02:49.518 --> 00:02:56.172
Next comes me. As I mentioned, the author Louisa and I share many traits.

28
00:02:56.173 --> 00:02:59.787
I am also a writer and I love to read.

29
00:02:59.788 --> 00:03:07.991
I'm not pretty like Meg or gentle like Beth, but I have a very strong personality, as my family will tell you.

30
00:03:07.992 --> 00:03:13.628
My biggest weak point is my short temper and I often lose control of it.

31
00:03:13.629 --> 00:03:18.397
It gets me into many arguments and sometimes causes mishaps.

32
00:03:18.398 --> 00:03:21.662
But I'm loyal and true to my family and friends.

33
00:03:21.663 --> 00:03:28.099
I will do anything for them. I'm a bit of a tomboy, which means I act like a boy.

34
00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:32.230
In fact, I'll admit I sometimes wish I were a boy.

35
00:03:32.231 --> 00:03:37.014
This kind of thinking also gets me into trouble.

36
00:03:37.015 --> 00:03:46.040
Beth is my darling little sister. I have a soft spot for her as she is the most gentle and shy creature you will ever come across.

37
00:03:46.041 --> 00:03:52.743
Like Mother, Beth is very caring and she holds nothing back when it comes to helping others.

38
00:03:52.744 --> 00:04:01.890
Beth never complains or upsets people and she would rather do something herself than be a bother to others. She loves music.

39
00:04:01.891 --> 00:04:06.559
Her voice is as angelic as her personality.

40
00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:10.674
Finally, there's Amy, the youngest of our clan.

41
00:04:10.675 --> 00:04:15.298
I suppose Amy and I are the pair of sisters who argue the most.

42
00:04:15.299 --> 00:04:19.470
Just between you and me, she irritates me so.

43
00:04:19.471 --> 00:04:23.816
However, I admit Amy does have her good traits.

44
00:04:23.817 --> 00:04:28.673
One of them is her beauty. She is like a porcelain doll.

45
00:04:28.674 --> 00:04:32.695
When she smiles at you, you forget all your troubles.

46
00:04:32.696 --> 00:04:35.954
She is also a very talented artist.

47
00:04:35.955 --> 00:04:40.694
I wouldn't be surprised if she became a famous painter one day.

48
00:04:40.695 --> 00:04:44.203
One of Amy's weaknesses is her selfishness.

49
00:04:44.204 --> 00:04:48.151
She's the youngest so I can understand this somewhat.

50
00:04:48.152 --> 00:04:55.663
But this characteristic gets her into several scrapes, which Amy thankfully learns from.

51
00:04:55.664 --> 00:05:01.295
So now you know a little about my family and something about Louisa May Alcott.

52
00:05:01.296 --> 00:05:06.374
As I mentioned before, our family lived during the American Civil War.

53
00:05:06.375 --> 00:05:10.984
Life at that time was quite different from what it is like for you today.

54
00:05:10.985 --> 00:05:14.432
For example, look at my clothes.

55
00:05:14.433 --> 00:05:23.477
Not only did we have to wear these long dresses, but when a woman went out, she was expected to wear gloves and carry a parasol.

56
00:05:23.478 --> 00:05:29.445
Given that I'm a tomboy, can you imagine how difficult it was for me to wear such things?

57
00:05:29.446 --> 00:05:35.269
My sisters had to remind me every time I wasn't dressed in a "ladylike" way.

58
00:05:35.270 --> 00:05:40.882
At this time, women were expected to behave in a certain manner as well.

59
00:05:40.883 --> 00:05:46.707
For most women, their purpose in life consisted of finding a marriage mate and having children.

60
00:05:46.708 --> 00:05:51.692
I resisted such notions and got myself into a lot of trouble for it.

61
00:05:51.693 --> 00:05:57.929
But I, like Louisa, am a firm believer that women should have their independence.

62
00:05:57.930 --> 00:06:02.241
Another thing you might find unusual is our way of life.

63
00:06:02.242 --> 00:06:06.138
It was common in our time to have servants and housekeepers.

64
00:06:06.139 --> 00:06:11.061
My family, as well as Louisa Alcott, hated the idea of slavery.

65
00:06:11.062 --> 00:06:14.703
We would never regard our beloved Hannah as a slave.

66
00:06:14.704 --> 00:06:20.392
She is trusted and loved and is a great help to our family.

67
00:06:20.393 --> 00:06:26.018
Something else you may find peculiar is how the young men and women interact.

68
00:06:26.019 --> 00:06:30.198
In my day, society was much more conservative.

69
00:06:30.199 --> 00:06:36.660
It was not considered proper for young people to date or go out unless they intended to marry.

70
00:06:36.661 --> 00:06:45.889
It's true that many married at a young age, but we had strict rules that allowed or did not allow certain behaviors.

71
00:06:45.890 --> 00:06:50.123
Time is constantly changing and that can't be helped.

72
00:06:50.124 --> 00:06:54.379
Fashions, manners, customs, and traditions change, too.

73
00:06:54.380 --> 00:07:04.250
Some things, however, are timeless: learning how to grow up, learning how to deal with family issues, learning to love and respect others,

74
00:07:04.251 --> 00:07:10.282
and of course─most important of all─learning who you are.

75
00:07:10.283 --> 00:07:14.503
Little Women is a story about just those things.

76
00:07:14.504 --> 00:07:17.790
Even though it was written more than a hundred years ago,

77
00:07:17.801 --> 00:07:28.158
I hope that you will find lessons you can learn from and apply in your life today.
